{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars","id":782288,"title":"Storytelling Solars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-08T07:17:09-08:00","id":782288,"title":"Storytelling Solars","content":"I have run more than a few games in my 27 years of life, and I like to think I'm at least passably good at it. From constructing interesting characters and narratives for PC's to interact with to offering characters opportunities for advancement growth and an equal share of the spotlight not just on my terms but also, perhaps most importantly, on the player's terms. I've run games for almost every splat in Exalted, except for a purely solar game-- which has always given me some trouble. <br /> <br /> Every other splat has a few clear &quot;points of attack&quot; of narrative handholds which unify the characters to some degree and create an excuse for their interaction and a shared set of &quot;interests or agendas&quot; or at least a set of subjects about which such things often develope. Not solars though, they can literally be anyone and care about anything (which is true for all characters but perhaps more so for solars who don't really have anything they must at least pay lip service to being concerned with and who also don't share any cultural social backgrounds) added to that their power makes them, at least it seems to me, better suited to 'sandbox' style games or games where central narratives or plots are initiated chiefly by them. While I like to give my player lots of latitude and I thrill to see them accomplish their goals and change their world (I ran a mountainfolk game once where the end goal I had plotted would result in a full scale mountainfolk invasion of the surface-- we didn't get there but it was a fun ride, and I ran a sidereal game where one of the players replaced a death lord incognito-- not at all my idea but an amazingly cool development) I find it difficult to prep for and therefor to run in an engaging manner sandbox style games with little to know overarching plot (and by plot i don't mean something I railroad the players into but rather to create a world for them filled with agents and actors with agendas for them to interact with) also the set up of &quot;you wander into a town where x is happening go&quot; always felt a bit thin to me. Beyond those two options I can only conceive of creating so many extraneous factions and plots that whatever the players do there is something there for them to interact with (which works on a case by case basis when a character's bio prompts me to create support for a plot hook they wrote in or where they state a goal they like to acheive but less so when things are super open ended). I guess what I'm asking is how do storytellers guide their solars through stories that are more Mass Effect or Elder Scrolls and less GTA in structure without just cramming it down their throats or preparing excessively for any eventuality? Are plot hooks of a smaller initial scale that work for lesser solars still appropriate for solars? How do you bring he circle together in an organic fashion? Players, what have storytellers done in the past that you particularly enjoyed?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:43:31-08:00","id":782295,"title":"","content":"You need something unifying the group, beyond the obvious &quot;we should stick together, in case of Wyld Hunt&quot;. In the groups I currently play in, we always set out to find some type of campaign we'd like to play, and then created characters that'd fit well together, trying not to step on each others toes too much. Maybe examples of the games I'm in might help.<br /> <br /> The basic ideas for our groups always came as a suggestion from one of the players and were:<br /> <br /> &quot;I want to basically create something like the grey wardens, protecting people from malicious forces like fair folk and undead and I'd like to play in the north.&quot;<br /> Everyone liked that idea, and went ahead to create someone who either would help build up such an organization, would share it's goals and help as an advisor or would lend his army to a good cause.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'd like to play something like Birthright, with every one of us either ruling a country or being a high priest or something. Lots of politics basically.&quot;<br /> Everyone liked the idea, and went ahead to create a sorcerer about to get fed up and go off to create their own, idyllic society, a highly influential diplomat who has the ear of her emperor or an entrepreneur who wants to create a modern corporation that spreads across Creation.<br /> <br /> Our third group is currently being debated, and has been for weeks, since we don't have a unifying idea everyone agrees with, so we've been playing one-shots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind is that every character still has his/her/it's own goals, in some cases at strong odds with other characters, but the unifying &quot;thingy&quot; is universally more important, so that they may end up fighting for a while, or torching each other's stuff but they'll, in the end, almost certainly revert to working together against bigger threats.<br /> <br /> When I am the storyteller, which currently I'm only in the one-shots group, I try to have a rough timeline for what happens around where the players are or what they hear of, from far away. Then I let things basically run simulationey, with the players able to avoid everything, if they so choose. I try to describe lots of mundane things, with no weird happenstances going on behind them.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's surprising which mundane thing catches their attention. I keep myself amused when I describe the mundane stuff by taking it from cultures I don't know a lot about (the fun's in the researching and sharing) or reading up on ones I haven't used in a while and throw in descriptions of things I found unusual or interesting, to give each place they visit some kind of personality.<br /> They still occasionally mention a place that they traveled through in a game over a year ago, simply for it having a special dish I described. It literally was nothing but &quot;the only interesting thing you come across in this small nation is &lt;insert dish&gt;&quot; To me it's sometimes baffling.<br /> <br /> So, basically my other suggestion is to throw minutae at them and see what sticks.<br /> At the very least, the next npc they ought not to overlook can ask for exactly that dish they liked so much or be wearing an outfit that looks just like what they found memorable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:52:47-08:00","id":782299,"title":"","content":"To distill my rant down to something more useful:<br /> Make sure you don't start the game, before everyone is on the same page about what kind of game you all want. And make sure to say no to ideas you just can't get thrilled about.<br /> I personally for example wouldn't accept &quot;well, basically adventurers&quot; as a concept. That's just not saying anything about what game they want. It also lays the burden on the ST to entertain them and somehow keep the game working, even if they end up with diametrically opposed expectations. I believe that's a recipe for disaster. That's what I was trying to convey per my examples, but I hope what I added here is more helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T08:13:43-08:00","id":782309,"title":"","content":"While there are stylistic factors to consider, I agree with Edward for my personal games. I like to pitch the concept for the main thrust of the plot, and then have people build characters that suit that concept and work well with each other. I then pull from their backstories to flesh out the game and to plan opportunities for specific character arcs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T08:19:39-08:00","id":782312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782309#post782309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there are stylistic factors to consider, I agree with Edward for my personal games. I like to pitch the concept for the main thrust of the plot, and then have people build characters that suit that concept and work well with each other. I then pull from their backstories to flesh out the game and to plan opportunities for specific character arcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly how I have run games in the past, was looking for validation that this structure was 'suitable' to a solar game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T08:28:14-08:00","id":782315,"title":"","content":"Absolutely! Coming to the table with an arc and a premise helps to avoid the diffusion of narrative thrust that can sometimes accompany the free-for-all nature of Solar characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T11:27:39-08:00","id":782404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars#post782288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Every other splat has a few clear &quot;points of attack&quot; of narrative handholds which unify the characters to some degree and create an excuse for their interaction and a shared set of &quot;interests or agendas&quot; or at least a set of subjects about which such things often develop. Not solars though</div> </div> </div> </div>As a player, I've found Solars less interesting than other splats... in part because of (IMO) the lack of handholds, the impression of repetitive events (ie roll a d4: 1 stumble into conflict, 2 bring down the establishment, 3 raid a tomb, 4 fight/flee a wyld hunt) and little existing 'culture'. Having realized the turn offs and experimented a little, I'm less of a &quot;Solars... yawn&quot; person now. Storytelling wise, Solars come with less compulsory baggage.... letting you tailor the scale and scope of a campaign. You could technically run a small town game with Sidereals or a save the world game with Dragonblooded, but its less work with Solars <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars#post782288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess what I'm asking is how do storytellers guide their solars through stories that are more Mass Effect or Elder Scrolls and less GTA in structure without just cramming it down their throats or preparing excessively for any eventuality? Are plot hooks of a smaller initial scale that work for lesser solars still appropriate for solars? How do you bring the circle together in an organic fashion? Players, what have storytellers done in the past that you particularly enjoyed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough I've never done the 'the current circle were also past circle mates' setup, which might well work for a game that focus a lot on past life events.<br /> <br /> Often I'm the sort of ST to use small scale plot hooks... to hint at the larger hooks, so if the small plot seems too easy accomplished then its not the end of world. For 3rd Ed, I'd like to shake up my style and try some new things.<br /> <br /> Usually forging some pre-game relationships between the characters works best for our group (unless the premise of the game relies on the characters not being acquainted). The Circle tends to form with a precedent of past co-operation (whether its due to friendships, prior business dealings, or reputation based) that usually carries over fairly well.<br /> <br /> Probably the most useful (to you) of our various enjoyable ST moments would be;<br /> 1) a set of very dynamic NPCs in an unusually exotic location (ie students &amp; teachers in a Dragonblooded 'school' game, set in the Palace of Tamed Storms).<br /> 2) taking a character's background trait and running it with amusing gusto, even though it had zero relevance to the game's plot (an Abyssal Necrosurgeon's retainer... her invalid father that craved true death, but was too cherished to be granted it).<br /> 3) a 'frame up' of the PCs that was cleverly executed and led to many other plots (hiring the PCs to capture an airship and steal some cargo... only to have the ship explode in mid-battle due to previous set explosives. It was later revealed to be carrying important people, setting empires on the brink of war).<br /> 4) rebuilding a cannon 'hero' into a villain (the Bull of the North was remade into a closet cannibal who overthrew his tribe, converted the survivors to his ways, and entered into an alliance with an outlawed Terrestrial goddess &quot;Sweet Surloin&quot;,.. who had taken on the identity of the deceased Samea).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Long time lurker","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8781-happy-hermit","name":"Happy Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8781_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T11:59:42-08:00","id":782416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars#post782288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess what I'm asking is how do storytellers guide their solars through stories that are more Mass Effect or Elder Scrolls and less GTA in structure without just cramming it down their throats or preparing excessively for any eventuality?</div> </div> </div> </div>You tell your players what you want and they help you do it. Then you help them create characters that work within that narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are plot hooks of a smaller initial scale that work for lesser solars still appropriate for solars? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you bring he circle together in an organic fashion? </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest you bring it together in a <i>dramatic</i> fashion.<br /> <br /> That said, if one of the player's has a social PC, ask them to help bring the circle together. You mentioned Mass Effect; the second ME was all about Commander Shepard gathering up people for a specific task.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:23:04-08:00","id":782434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars#post782288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have run more than a few games in my 27 years of life, an-.</div> </div> </div> </div>GOD DAMNIT. Now I feel like an old bastard.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:25:45-08:00","id":782436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782434#post782434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> GOD DAMNIT. Now I feel like an old bastard.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps I'm actually 28-- I don't know why I keep forgetting that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:39:57-08:00","id":782444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782434#post782434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> GOD DAMNIT. Now I feel like an old bastard.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 22. <br /> <br /> *Flees to the fields of youth*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T13:06:03-08:00","id":782454,"title":"","content":"I had this problem when planning my current game. Everyone wanted to do radically different things and I couldn't decide how to link the party together, so I just ended up embracing the sandbox. All our characters are mobile for different reasons, so games will take place when everyone ends up in the same town &quot;by chance&quot; just as shit is about to go down. We'll see how long it takes them to realize that sidereals are fucking with them.<br /> <br /> The important thing to remember is that characters will generally work together to get through adversity so long as they aren't ideologically opposed on key issues. Just keep the adversity flowing and eventually the party will either kill each other or become friends and you can lay off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:41:01-08:00","id":782509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782436#post782436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps I'm actually 28-- I don't know why I keep forgetting that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. I've been running games longer than you've been alive...<br /> <br /> On topic, I'm with Monkipi and Edward. The current game started as a first age &quot;extended prelude&quot; then we switched systems and made the Age of Sorrows incarnations of the original circle. The first Story arc is relatively tightly scripted - not to railroading levels, but I have a definate story that isn't related to the PC's goals. Primarily because my players tend to take a while to figure out what those are. After that story arc is done, I'll go with pursuing their goals and interweaving troubles caused by the now deathlord Big Bad of the prelude.<br /> <br /> We also adapted part of the FATE character creation rules, having everyone exchange backgrounds and come up with how their character crossed the paths of two others, which worked well, even if they already had the common element of having been trained at the same dojo (which teaches several different Martial Art Styles)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:43:42-08:00","id":782513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782436#post782436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps I'm actually 28-- I don't know why I keep forgetting that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still making me feel old. I just turned 3* a week ago <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:50:40-08:00","id":782518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782454#post782454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All our characters are mobile for different reasons, so games will take place when everyone ends up in the same town &quot;by chance&quot; just as shit is about to go down. We'll see how long it takes them to realize that sidereals are fucking with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My PCs just realized that perhaps it wasn't just random chance that caused all four of them to wander into the same mountain valley while seeking refuge from the Northern winters....<br /> <br /> Personally, I like to go for an escalating scale for Solars. Start small - get to know some local village, build ties there, defend it from something menacing it (in my current case a neighboring tribe looking to sell some slaves to the Guild and/or House Cynis). Gradually expand to a larger scale - troubles at the village lead the PCs to the seat of the local satrapy, where they have considerably higher stakes, but still anchored in the attachments they've made. Defeat what looks like the main villain, only to find out there was something much worse waiting in the wings. - Suddenly the PCs find out what those Realm troops they ran off were protecting against.<br /> <br /> And all the while, I try to keep exploring themes like what it really means to be a hero, how the easy answer isn't always the best, and the law of unintended consequences. Hooray, you slaughtered the Realm patrol that was harassing travelers. Which means they're not in town to help when the beastmen attack.<br /> <br /> I also generally see a Solar game going in 3 acts:<br /> Act 1 - scrabbling for resources, few to no allies, have to be EXTREMELY careful about not showing off what you are, never know who to trust, terrified of a Wyld Hunt descending on you at any moment. - This tends to be more plot driven and less sandboxy<br /> Act 2 - Solars start to come into their own. They have found/made a home for themselves where they don't need to fear every peasant running for the local Immaculate as soon as an anima pops. Begin consolidating power. Still have to be careful though, lest in their hubris everything get knocked down. - this is where the sandbox generally opens up.<br /> Act 3 - Climax. The big showdown with a Deathlord/main Raksha villain/major Realm power/etc.<br /> <br /> I generally spend most of my time on Acts 1 and 2, with 3 really being mostly the big payoff for all the buildup before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8899-vayaconqueso","name":"VayaConQueso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T16:04:17-08:00","id":782540,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of your quasi-historical fantasy anime of the last few years can give a good sense for the structure of a story that could fit into a given part of Creation (or even a number of parts in sequence); a land in some kind of crisis that brings a diverse group together and sends them roving about trying to solve such crisis in the face of complex issues, varied personages and powerful institutions. Stuff like Heroic Legend of Arslan, Yona of the Dawn, Lord Marksman and Vanadis, Magi, those kinds of things. They might be particularly good for helping one imagine how to chain the locations of the sandbox together with common themes or recurring images. I think once one has a sense for how the things look at the surface level, it's not necessary to make them too intricate; for any given locale that the players visit, you can modify details in the appearance of the place and the names and face of the figures, and take advantage of Quick Character improvisation to throw up local soldiers and their masters, and the thing is kept from being too expansive by the sense of what problems people are facing regardless of where you go, and the idea that whatever the challenges the players overcome, they're breaking things down such that new things can prop up (probably things that might require a revisit at a few points).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T17:25:53-08:00","id":782561,"title":"","content":"With the new system, I don't think it's unreasonable to say &quot;you have to have some kind of non-antagonistic Intimacy towards at least two other members of your Circle,&quot; as rationale for sticking around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T21:06:19-08:00","id":782606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782561#post782561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the new system, I don't think it's unreasonable to say &quot;you have to have some kind of non-antagonistic Intimacy towards at least two other members of your Circle,&quot; as rationale for sticking around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree. One of my first requirements when we made characters was that everyone had to have a positive Intimacy towards at least one if not more of their circlemates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8899-vayaconqueso","name":"VayaConQueso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T14:31:32-08:00","id":783054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VayaConQueso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=782606#post782606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally agree. One of my first requirements when we made characters was that everyone had to have a positive Intimacy towards at least one if not more of their circlemates.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While helpful, that kinda limits concepts for characters. I tend to present a concept or cause for the characters, and require them to find a way to support that.<br /> <br /> I also sit down with each player individually and go over their backstory, Intimacies, etc, and if I see a problem, I point t it and say &quot;Explain to me how this will make you better able to work with your fellow PCs when you meet.&quot; That addresses the problem in a hurry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T17:34:06-08:00","id":783152,"title":"","content":"I found, honestly, that making people take intimacies to each other and have a past background together, doesn't actually work very well if it turns out the characters have very different goals and methodologies. Because they just argue and lose their intimacies.<br /> Ideological similarities work better. For example, several of the characters are anti-slavery, or anti-Realm, or pro-Cult of the Illuminated, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T21:16:47-08:00","id":783224,"title":"","content":"The circle-ties idea can work I think, if you are clear that a positive tie can be basically <i>any</i> non-antagonistic emotion. Characters might be friends, co-workers, competitors, lovers, partners in crime or anything else. You can also encourage background that doesn't necessarily result in ties, like how Solar A never quite forgave Solar B for the losses they took fighting off the realm in Town C, or characters might have had romantic feelings at one point that have puttered out, and others.<br /> <br /> A shared story at starting is a good idea, which may or may not require intimacies, but history is important for PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T03:58:08-08:00","id":783353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=783054#post783054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While helpful, that kinda limits concepts for characters. I tend to present a concept or cause for the characters, and require them to find a way to support that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hardly consider one positive tie an onerous burden on concept. I find it useful because Exalted doesn't work well on the D&amp;D or Shadowrub tropes of &quot;everyone meets in a bar when hired for the same job&quot; or standard group meet-up reasons for a number of other games, mainly because of the power level of starting characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T04:53:38-08:00","id":783375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=783353#post783353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hardly consider one positive tie an onerous burden on concept. I find it useful because Exalted doesn't work well on the D&amp;D or Shadowrub tropes of &quot;everyone meets in a bar when hired for the same job&quot; or standard group meet-up reasons for a number of other games, mainly because of the power level of starting characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally did this. Everyone met in a teahouse, got into a brawl, tried to run away, and then a Sidereal came along, and there was no brawl, and they always knew each other, and no Sidereals were involved, and Sidereals do not exist.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal doesn't know they are Solars, though. She was just told to make sure they had reason to stick together. So far, no one is complaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T05:17:12-08:00","id":783384,"title":"","content":"My group currently was not required to have a positive intimacy towards each other, but they are all close friends IRL, so most of them put it on their character sheets anyway. For prepping for me group I did a first age group prologue where they were invited to a dinner with some fellow solars that did not go so well, and they fought their way to Rathiss, where they all eventually died due to Sidereal backstabbing. I brought the group together by using their individual prologues for gold faction maneuvering, they all were basically instructed to meet in the same village, and each of them was promised something that would interest them. At this point I deviated from Exalted and had the group come up with Interludes from Savage Worlds. They told me how the meet, what mini adventure they had together, etc. It seemed to work well for my group, and gave me more RP fodder for down the road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2249-ahopa","name":"Ahopa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T05:29:38-08:00","id":783387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=783375#post783375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I literally did this. Everyone met in a teahouse, got into a brawl, tried to run away, and then a Sidereal came along, and there was no brawl, and they always knew each other, and no Sidereals were involved, and Sidereals do not exist.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal doesn't know they are Solars, though. She was just told to make sure they had reason to stick together. So far, no one is complaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. For me, personally, it's a little too much IC fiat. I like characters to have ties because, to me, it makes plot development easier and more likely that people actually want to help rather than feeling like &quot;this is the plot we got and my character wouldn't be that interested because these people are basically strangers but I want to play today so may as well go.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-10-2015, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T05:51:41-08:00","id":783396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=783353#post783353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hardly consider one positive tie an onerous burden on concept. I find it useful because Exalted doesn't work well on the D&amp;D or Shadowrub tropes of &amp;quot;everyone meets in a bar when hired for the same job&amp;quot; or standard group meet-up reasons for a number of other games, mainly because of the power level of starting characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I suppose that depends on the scale of the job, I could certainly see a solar working to support a local monarch (especially one he had a great deal of faith in before his exaltation) there is nothing that says solars can't be body guards and mercenaries or village blacksmiths (who also make items of wonder alongside new cribs for local children and shoes for the town's horses). Solars are people first after all. More over if someone were recruiting solars to perform an oceans 11 style heist on the imperial manse or some other big fear, the presence of more than one solar might not strain credulity too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T05:55:19-08:00","id":783399,"title":"","content":"I like having the characters being linked... but, honestly, I find that in practice it doesn't work that well. Things that happened before the game just don't have the same impact. And frequently characters quickly evolve into something slightly different from what they're supposed to.<br /> If it doesn't seem believable from the characters' interaction, intimacies don't tend to hold up.<br /> <br /> For example, I played a game where me and my friend's character were good friends in the past, and he saved my character's life. But then, when we played the game, that character constantly insulted my character (and everyone else) and her beliefs and culture (mostly out of ignorance), and crapped up a lot of our missions and goals. It made it a bit difficult to see why they were best friends.<br /> <br /> Similarly, when I first ran Exalted, I gave all the Lunars a Solar mate amongst the PCs. With some Lunars it worked well, with others it made literally no difference whatsoever. Just having an intimacy written on their sheet didn't make the player care about the other character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T05:55:48-08:00","id":783400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=783387#post783387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;this is the plot we got and my character wouldn't be that interested because these people are basically strangers but I want to play today so may as well go.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it probably helped that we all created characters together, and figured out how they would actually interact during the game, and how their intimacies and personalities would work. The players also suggested the other possible intimacies, which were usually accepted. It's just that the actual meeting was &quot;what's a Sidereal&quot;, because it helped me get the players acquainted with the stuff that can happen to Exalts, or around Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T05:59:14-08:00","id":783401,"title":"","content":"I want to expand a bit on what I said before:<br /> I said that I don't find giving people ties is necessarily that useful.<br /> What I do find is that having people be similar ideologically is useful. For example, the same religion, the same philosophy, the same goals.<br /> Which is why making characters somewhat together can work reasonably well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T06:11:27-08:00","id":783406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/782288-storytelling-solars?p=783400#post783400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it probably helped that we all created characters together, and figured out how they would actually interact during the game, and how their intimacies and personalities would work. The players also suggested the other possible intimacies, which were usually accepted. It's just that the actual meeting was &amp;quot;what's a Sidereal&amp;quot;, because it helped me get the players acquainted with the stuff that can happen to Exalts, or around Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That all sounds awesome. I am a huge proponent of groups having a &quot;Session Zero,&quot; just so everyone is on the same page and similar expectations for tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T07:09:55-08:00","id":783423,"title":"","content":"I am also a huge proponent of session zeros. Even when groups have been together for a long time they help to set tone and expectations. The session zero for my present campaign involved establishing how everyone came to know each other, and actually ultimately fueled us with the plot hook with spurred us into the campaign.<br /> <br /> Especially as it pertains to expectation-setting though, I think they are important. My group is a bunch of faffy narrativist story people (I say this as the worst of them) and one more &quot;traditional&quot; player we've been playing with for a while now, to everyone's enjoyment. We did, however, have to have conversations about his mechanical choices, how they reflected his character arc, etc. The biggest stumbling block was that he still has assumptions of antagonistic STing, and we really had to set the record straight on that one. Without the session zero, we would have been dealing with a pretty large mismatch in concepts and assumptions at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T18:53:50-08:00","id":786415,"title":"","content":"How do I run Solar games? Great question. I get the players together to give them an idea about where in Creation the game will begin and take place. Giving them a location gives them a culture to build characters from. We talk about the characters to make sure abilities compliment each other and that there isn't a gaping ability hole (&quot;No one has any short range combat options?!&quot;).<br /> <br /> I also like to have the players write up a backstory. Often this gives me plot hooks and interesting story ideas that I run with and eventually mesh into other characters' back stories. Additionally, I'll often make it so that the characters' previous incarnations were either Circlemates or well acquainted in the First Age. This seems to give the Solars a foundation to build trust upon without the unnatural feeling of forcing characters who don't know each other (and players who don't yet know their own characters) into sudden immediate friendship.<br /> <br /> I've learned to love the sandbox style games Solar stories often become. I've also learned not to spend hours developing what I think to be an interesting NPC only to have the Solars change course and never encounter him/her or whack said NPC into oblivion upon first meeting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T19:02:02-08:00","id":786422,"title":"","content":"I have used this as a guiding light for years for Solar games:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey C. Grabowski</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &gt;&gt;&gt;Exactly what do the Solar Exalted end up doing in the world, and how do they do it?&lt;&lt;&lt;<br /> <br /> The same thing as heroes in our world -- perform great deeds, conquer kingdoms, wage lavish wars for love or ideology.<br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt;As I said, this is likely my stupid question, but as I read through the book, I just keep getting the image of any exalting Solar being quickly killed by the locals and the Dragon-Blooded, or quickly pressed into service of a Deathlord or major spirit.&lt;&lt;&lt;<br /> <br /> Well, it's like this. Many of them do get killed, or kill themselves. That's why the default character is several years post-Exaltation; so that the &quot;oh my god what am I and how do I hide?!&quot; plotline is over.<br /> <br /> Also, consider this: you meet an infant god. Do you enthrall it so you can suffer its unending wrath in 200 years when it grows to the fullness of its power? Even if it can't escape, sooner or later some other Solar or Lunar is going to come along and gack you to make sure that nobody thinks this sort of foolishness is an option. Obviously, some people will say &quot;hell yeah!&quot; and try to slap you in chains anyway, but there are some persuasive arguments why trying to immediately enthrall every Exalt you meet is a bad idea, and they're hardly unequipped<br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt;Now, assuming that I don't particularly want to start off any game that I might center around Solar characters with either their death or the complete and continual subjugation to some greater power, what would the Solar do?&lt;&lt;&lt;<br /> <br /> Lay low and try to gather power without making a spectacle of herself? Try to find gods and Exalts willing to be allies rather than masters? Not everyone plays out of the Machivellian side of the court. There's always lovers and idealists, at the very least. Finally, a careful Solar can be pretty open. Who's going to come stop you? As long as your supernatural neighbors support you and you don't park yourself on someone's strategic interest or start to look like a serious competititor to a global or regional power, people are going to care about as much as they do in the real world. The power-players in Creation have other things to worry about. In the cracks between their spheres of interest is where Solars can take root and establish powerbases. It's when they try to translate themselves into a regional power that things get ugly.<br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt;And on a slightly related note, is there a particular good thematic reason for keeping the Limit Break/angst angle of the Solars? For some reason, that just keeps striking me as out of character for the game...&lt;&lt;&lt;<br /> <br /> Not at all. Actual heroes from actual epics make all sorts of irrational and bad decisions. Limit break and the great Curse, while they're nice additions to the game's Big Story, are mostly just there to provide an &quot;in-setting&quot; justification for people who go &quot;but my character would /never/ do that!&quot; when in fact they should.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T02:10:37-08:00","id":787928,"title":"","content":"In my old campaign the first session could be summed uo as: &quot;You are all people from modern-day Earth who exalt as Solars and then have to flee through a Portal to Creation, stranding you in the High Lands of An-Teng. Now what do you do?&quot;<br /> <br /> That seemed to work for getting them to stick together.<br /> <br /> (For those who are interested in the details, I am currently re-doing this campaign <a href=\"http://german-geek.blogspot.de/search/label/there%20and%20back%20again?m=0\" target=\"_blank\">as an actual sandbox </a>, though it's mostly an intellectual exercise right now.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}